        return -1;   /* reject out‑of‑range lengths */
    size = user_len;
    void *buf = malloc(size);
    if (!buf)
        return -1;
    return buf;
}
```
- The check uses both signed (`SIZE_MAX`) and unsigned (`SIZE`) limits.
- It ensures that adding any header size does not wrap around.
- Allocation now occurs only after safe validation.

